# Vault index for Claude

This file is imported by `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, so it is in context in every session. It lists the
projects kept in this vault.

## How to use this

- When a task belongs to a project below, read `<Path>/README.md`, then `<Path>/claude/README.md`,
  before anything else. The second one holds the project's rules, skills and agents.
- Before reading or writing notes, run `second-brain conventions` and follow it. The full note is
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/obsidian-conventions.md`.
- Your own skills and agents live in `claude/` at the vault root and in each project's `claude/`
  folder. `claude/README.md` says how to add one.
- Plugin skills: `story-tracker` tracks tasks, `sprint` runs a sprint, `vault-setup` sets up the
  vault or a project, `vault-doctor` checks them. Plugin agents: `scrum-master` for the sprint
  cadence, `docs-keeper` for docs that follow the code.
- If a task belongs to none of these projects, ignore this file.

## Rules that most often go wrong

- A task is always `<project>/tasks/<TICKET-ID>/README.md`. Never file it inside the topic it is
  about; tie it to the topic with a tag that is the folder path, lowercased.
- A bare `[[Alias]]` does not resolve. Links carry a path:
  `[[<vault path or unique file name>|<alias>]]`.
- Move and rename notes with the helper (`second-brain move`, `second-brain rename`), never `mv`.
- Frontmatter is the truth. Read a status from the `status` property, never from prose.

